\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Let earth and heaven agree,
\par Angels and men be joined,
\par To celebrate with me
\par The Saviour of mankind;
\par To adore the all-atoning Lamb,
\par And bless the sound of Jesu's name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Jesus, transporting sound!
\par The joy of earth and heaven;
\par No other help is found,
\par No other name is given,
\par By which we can salvation have;
\par But Jesus came the world to save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus, harmonious name!
\par It charms the hosts above;
\par They evermore proclaim
\par And wonder at His love;
\par 'Tis all their happiness to gaze,
\par 'Tis heaven to see our Jesu's face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. His name the sinner hears;
\par And is from sin set free;
\par 'Tis music in his ears,
\par 'Tis life and victory;
\par New songs do now his lips employ,
\par And dances his glad heart for joy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Stung by the scorpion sin,
\par My poor expiring soul
\par The healing sound drinks in,
\par And is at once made whole:
\par See there my Lord upon the tree!
\par I hear, I feel, He died for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O unexampled love!
\par O all-redeeming grace!
\par How swiftly didst Thou move
\par To save a fallen race:
\par What shall I do to make it known
\par What Thou for all mankind hast done?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O for a trumpet voice,
\par On all the world to call!
\par To bid their hearts rejoice
\par In Him who died for all;
\par For all my Lord was crucified,
\par For all, for all my saviour died.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

